Subject: windows.ui.xaml: OnWindowCreated, LeavingBackground, Window.VisibilityChanged and Windows.UI.Text.FontWeights

Application.OnWindowCreated is called with WindowCreatedEventArgs once the main window exists (in
IFrameworkView.SetWindow, before OnLaunched), as WinUI does. Xbox Accessories starts its device layer there; with
it never called, its DeviceManager stayed "NotReady" and its pages waited for device discovery forever.

Application.LeavingBackground is raised after the first activation (OnLaunched) with LeavingBackgroundEventArgs
whose deferral completes at once. Window.VisibilityChanged (Visible) is raised when Activate shows the window, just
before Activated. Windows.UI.Text.FontWeights gives the named weights.

